{"text": "January 3, 2019\n\n\u2018Tim Sullivan, CEO\nNew Jersey Economic Development Authority\n16 W. State Street\nTrenton, NI\n\nDear Tim:\n\ntes with a mixture of regret and relief that | submit my resignation as Vice President of Policy, Planning\nand Research. | feel very fortunate that | had this opportunity to serve the residents of New Jersey and\nbbe a part of such a smart and dedicated team here at the Economic Development Authority. |am very\nproud of what we accomplished over the last year. | know there isso much more work to be done.\n\nUnfortunately, since the fal, | have experienced a certain level of retaliation from members of the\nadministration that is keeping me from doing my job effectively, including exclusions from meetings and\nbeing prevented from working on projects that | had been assigned to earlier this year. That\ndiscrimination and hostility, and the lack of support here, have been frustrating and draining, and | have\nchosen to leave my position to protect my health and happiness. As corny as it sounds, | came into this\n\u2018administration aspiring to make the world a better place and feel | can do that somewhere else much\n\u2018more productively and without the unnecessary stress and strain.\n\n' hope the EDA team will have great success in implementing the state economic strategy that we\ndeveloped this year. | propose to stay through the end of January to work with my department and\nothers here to ensure a smooth transition,\n\nSincerely,",
